roup of \\mathbb F_p by the group of points of an elliptic curve over \\mathbb F_p. By Hasse's theorem [Sil2009, Theorem V.1.1] its order lies in [p + 1 - 2\\sqrt p, p + 1 + 2\\sqrt p], and as the curve varies the order is distributed over this interval roughly like a random integer of that size. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpeeding the Pollard and Elliptic Curve Methods of Factorization | CiNii Research (https://cir.nii.ac.jp/crid/1362825894414381824)\nciteturn3search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Speeding the Pollard and Elliptic Curve Methods of Factorization ... Montgomery ... Mathematics of Computation 48 (177), 243-, 1987-01\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nrpb097 (https://maths-people.anu.edu.au/brent/pub/pub097.html)\nciteturn3search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 41.2 years ago; Crawled: 13.8 years ago; Brent, Some integer factorization algorithms using elliptic curves, Report CMA-R32-85, Centre for Mathematical Analysis, ANU, September 1985, ii+19 pp.\n\nAbstract: dvi (2K), pdf (76K), ps (26K). ... We mention some refinements which give greater speedup, an alternative way of implementing a second phase, and the connection with Pollard's \"p-1\" factorization algorithm. ... This Technical Report was a preliminary (longer) version of Brent [102], and was one of the first publications on Hendrik Lenstra's elliptic curve method. ... Equations (7.3) and (7.7) have obvious (easily corrected) errors.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nElliptic Curves with the Montgomery (https://doczz.net/doc/7731857/elliptic-curves-with-the-montgomery)\nciteturn3search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 26.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     while Montgomery originally introduced this type of curves for speeding\n    up the Pollard and Elliptic Curve Methods of integer factorization [Math. ... Vol.48, No.177, (1987) pp